    "body": "## Reproduced source/import mismatch\n\nOwner: `estate-6267db2cfc6e/root`, under Jacob's continuing HAMON estate execution mandate, with independent receiving by `authority_recovery`.\n\nAt current main `e2285d68b2ea5eb2158c0a7e0d936ce5d56f8ff5` (tree `22da6a890c2befaf72d3826103538491b07793df`), `testpilot/diff.py::module_name` strips a leading `lib/` as though it were an import root. The actual sandbox adds only the repository's `src/` directory, when present, and repository root to `PYTHONPATH`; the README documents those same roots.\n\nThe frozen independent witness uses the exact current `diff.py` and `sandbox.py`, actual function selection, and five fresh Python import processes through the unchanged sandbox runner. It reports **three assertion failures, two passing controls and zero errors**:\n\n- `lib/pricing.py` is selected with module `pricing`, which is unimportable when only the selected package exists.\n- With a root-level namesake, the suggested import resolves the wrong source/value (99 rather than the selected function's 2).\n- A changed `lib/__init__.py` receives an empty module name.\n- Ordinary root-package and `src/lib/` package controls pass.\n\nSource and fixture bytes remain unchanged. Baseline receiving SHA-256: `690a606509ecb737a01c18b0cefad41bf05e96b6a7e67b6139ed8c42001e6be0`. Loader source blob: `f92280a9ad3f9f79713dce7ba7ae28c55414783a`; sandbox source blob: `dd6b25f1a93bc6f313ae8c8d01ede5ba83440b5b`.\n\n## Narrow contribution boundary\n\nPreserve the leading `lib` package component while retaining the existing one-level `src/` handling. Scope is `testpilot/diff.py::module_name`, a new focused `tests/test_module_identity.py`, a small import-identity guide, and uniquely named source-bound qualification evidence.\n\nFresh ownership review found that #30 explicitly preserves `diff.py` and the automatic selector; #29 owns report staging, #28 saved-test recheck, and #26 saved-run comparison. This contribution leaves those implementations with their owners and requires no provider/model call.\n\nFreeze the regression before editing production, qualify the original failure and repaired import identity through the real consumer path, run the relevant existing tests and normal repository CI, obtain independent receiving, then integrate against freshly reviewed main.\n",
